DSpark drafter provenance

config.py and model.py were imported byte-for-byte from the MIT-licensed
mlx-dspark project, and loader.py adapts that project's load.py to
vllm-metal's model lifecycle. The source, at commit
9e39ea2fdc6d99d855af2cb7ef9933391c4391db, is:

https://github.com/ARahim3/mlx-dspark/tree/9e39ea2fdc6d99d855af2cb7ef9933391c4391db/src/mlx_dspark

All three files have since been modified here (checkpoint validation, memory
bounds and serving integration) and keep MIT headers naming the original
copyright holder. The rest of this package, the proposer and the target
capture are original to vllm-metal under the repository's Apache-2.0 license.

mlx-dspark is an independent MLX implementation that contains no DeepSpec
source code; DeepSeek-AI/DeepSpec (MIT) is the official numerical reference for
the drafter. No model weights are bundled: the Qwen3 targets and the DSpark
drafter checkpoints are downloaded at runtime under their publishers' licenses.

